Construction & Civilian - Mason
Traditional multipurpose wall and civil engineering
Full time Interinale
Candidate
Apply for this job
Traditional multipurpose wall and civil engineering
* indicates mandatory fields
Do you want the freedom of temporary work and the safety of permanent employment?
For 30 years, we have been supporting hundreds of companies in the technical sectors of construction, construction and industry throughout Switzerland, offering them the best talents.
We will not lie to you, but we are demanding. So, if you are a motivated and extremely enthusiastic person, join our team for the location of traditional multipurpose Muratore and civil engineering
Your assignment:
- Perform several traditional masonry and civil engineering works in various yards;
- Perform construction, restructuring and processing;
- Building walls, partitions, foundations, floors and concrete works;
- Make laying bricks, concrete blocks, perforated blocks and various masonry elements;
- Participating in the construction, reinforcement and casting of concrete;
- Concrete and finishing works;
- Intervention on civil engineering works such as ropes, wells, conduits, walls and small works;
- Work on restructuring, transformation and restoration of existing works;
- To read and interpret construction projects and technical documents;
- Perform finishing work and ensure the quality of the works made;
- Use the tools and equipment necessary for the various works correctly;
- Adapting to the different tasks and needs of the yard;
- Respect safety standards and construction procedures;
- Working in collaboration with the team leader and the different operators;
- Keep the equipment and work area clean and in good condition.
And now we're talking about you?
- Consolidated experience as a multipurpose bricklayer;
- Mastery of traditional masonry and civil engineering techniques;
